	(text "I burnt IO14 \non some boards,\nso for flexibility\nI will not use it"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 91.44 84.074 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "04ad1513-4263-46ec-8683-3eb3d8359908")
	)
	(text "The LED_* here are controlling a\nMOSFET 2N7000's gate on the other side.\nThey operate at 3.3V.\nThe BTN_* on the other side are just a \n100nF debounce cap and they close to GND, \nso we pull them up to 3.3V.\nThe 5V is to power the LED, and the MOSFET \nopen/closes the GND path on the power."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.464 215.646 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "19e9ffd5-cde3-4151-b703-874f8c8d4d96")
	)
	(text "S3 pin notes:\n\nIO14 --> I burnt down on some early chips, avoid if can\nIO3 --> strapping pin for JTAG\nit only does anything if you've burned the \nJTAG-select eFuse, so on a stock chip it's inert\n\nIO34 --> \nonly free when the module uses quad flash/PSRAM; \non octal parts (ESP32-S3R8) they're wired to the extra SPI \ndata lines and are off-limits.\nOn the LOLIN S3 which has the ESP32-S3FH4R2 it's ok since \nthe PSRAM is the R2 (2 MB) quad. But it's tied to the \nspecific memory variant. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.336 58.166 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "21d3d49a-f2df-472f-b292-97602f68c2cd")
	)
	(text "Optical enc is used to be +5V,\njust should run fine at +3.3V\nTCH is normally opened,\nand GND when closed.\nClosed it has a 33ohms R to GND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 327.406 225.806 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5ccece00-cb72-4538-8895-e665a89c490b")
	)
	(text "The OneButton's CH32V003 has \nLVTTL for pin voltage detection,\nso it can read 3.3V in.\nV_IH min is 2.06V when powered by 5V\nV_IL max is 1.09 V (low side)\nWe're good sending it 3.3V TX, with margins"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 288.29 70.358 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "61e014a8-f7a2-47f2-a998-9d9aa226d0cb")
	)
	(text "This comes back from the \nOneButton boards as 5V,\nand would fry the S3 so \nI have a divider down to 3.24V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 296.672 37.592 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "78311c2a-5cf4-4282-9593-a4eb2e1fcaf8")
	)
	(text "This pinout matches\nthe encoder's pinout\nif I mount a JST-PH\nangled on its bottom \nside.\nEnc is a KY-040"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 374.396 142.494 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9df43561-33aa-4fea-9b78-e7d8b9f38d20")
	)
	(text "Pi's layout is:\nFunction : GND | TX | RX\nGPIO     : 8   | 10 | 12\nPi sends in 3.3V and \nreceives ONLY 3.3V, \nso we natively good"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 98.044 131.826 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrainsMono NF")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c6f760c8-2acb-476d-9eaa-56ad4ab35274")
	)
	(text "Originally meant for 5V, \nbut fully passive potentiometer, \nso works at 3.3V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 69.85 231.902 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f43948bb-437f-4d5c-9d21-8918dcd36c62")
	)
